   It sounds "fun" (in the Nethack sense of the word), but it's definitely
a bug if, as the OP implied, it causes any of the following misbehaviors:

   (1) You can fall into the Quest and encounter the nemesis before
attaining the proper experience level.

   (2) You can fall into the Quest, kill the nemesis, return to the home
level, chat with the leader, and get a message to the effect of "Welcome
to the Quest. I wonder if you'll be able to kill the nemesis?" when in
fact you've already done so.

   (3) You can fall into the second level of the Quest, go upstairs to
the first level, and get a message to the effect of "You descend the
stairs to the first level of the Quest..." when in fact you're not
descending, and the message shouldn't appear at all.

   I agree that trapdoors alone would be a "nice" surprise for the player,
but they seem to have ramifications that the DevTeam didn't think of,
and /those/ qualify as bugs that need fixing. (Unless I'm mistaken about
all of 1,2,3 above.)

